(4417166, 632204, 66384, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective, and I like the bright yellow and blue together. What''s that tall modern squared off house doing on that nice old street?</td>', 'Nice perspective, and I like the bright yellow and blue together. What''s that tall modern squared off house doing on that nice old street?', '2008-01-23 10:03:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4417173, 632112, 66384, '<td valign="top">No wonder you got a ribbon for this. Great perspective, wonderful focus, interesting angle and beautiful color. Congratulations!</td>', 'No wonder you got a ribbon for this. Great perspective, wonderful focus, interesting angle and beautiful color. Congratulations!', '2008-01-23 10:08:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4417189, 633811, 75651, '<td valign="top">WOW... 4 favs.  That means so much more to me than the score itself.  Thank you everyone for your kind words.  I appreciate it very very much.<br/> <br/>Actually, here''s the funny part- his name is Zoe.  Whenever I take photos, he jumps up and sits oh so regally in front of the lens and is so good for the camera.  He is not a black cat however as most of you thought.  He is actually a Russian Blue with numorous shades of gray and blue.  I had a few of him playing with the band and biting and clawing the band, but this one, with the bright yellow eye in the middle, stood out for me.  It fell off his ear numourous times too, but he stayed there and let me put it back on.  <br/> <br/><i>NO TREATS WE USED IN THE PHOTOGRAPHING OF THIS ANIMAL</i>. He is a very patient and regal cat. Unlike my other cat "J i n x".  Check her out in the self-entitled photo.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the favs and the comments again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-23 20:24:12.</i></td>', 'WOW... 4 favs.  That means so much more to me than the score itself.  Thank you everyone for your kind words.  I appreciate it very very much. Actually, here''s the funny part- his name is Zoe.  Whenever I take photos, he jumps up and sits oh so regally in front of the lens and is so good for the camera.  He is not a black cat however as most of you thought.  He is actually a Russian Blue with numorous shades of gray and blue.  I had a few of him playing with the band and biting and clawing the band, but this one, with the bright yellow eye in the middle, stood out for me.  It fell off his ear numourous times too, but he stayed there and let me put it back on.   NO TREATS WE USED IN THE PHOTOGRAPHING OF THIS ANIMAL. He is a very patient and regal cat. Unlike my other cat "J i n x".  Check her out in the self-entitled photo. Thank you for the favs and the comments again.', '2008-01-23 10:13:47.000000', '2008-01-23 20:24:12.000000', 0),
